WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:04.710
- [Instructor] So we are
given this function h of x,

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.530
and we're asked, over which interval

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:12.140
does h have a positive
average rate of change?

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.280
So like always, pause this
video and have a go at it

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.180
before we do this together.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.560
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.680
And to start, let's just remind ourselves

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.830
what an average rate of change even is.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.980
You can view it as, the change
in your value of the function

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:34.970
for a given change in
the underlying variable

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.400
for a given change in x.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.760
We could also view this as,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.290
if we wanna figure out the interval,

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:43.700
we could say our x final
minus our x initial,

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.230
and in the numerator, it would
be the value of our function

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:51.000
at the x final, minus
the value of the function

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.700
at our x initial.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.210
Now they aren't asking
us to calculate this

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.320
for all of these different intervals.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.230
They're just asking us
whether it is positive.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:01.810
And if you look over here,

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:05.530
as long as our x final is
greater than x initial,

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:08.360
in order to have a positive
average rate of change,

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.670
we just need to figure
out whether h at x final

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:17.450
is greater than h at x initial.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.410
If the value of the function
at the higher endpoint

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:22.870
is larger than the value of the function

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:23.720
at the lower endpoint,

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.930
then we have a positive
average rate of change.

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:31.050
So let's see if that's happening
for any of these choices.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:34.260
So let's see, h of zero,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:38.450
this endpoint, is going
to be equal to zero.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.100
If I just say 1/8 times zero minus zero,

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.411
and h of two is equal to 1/8

00:01:46.411 --> 00:01:49.936
times two to the third power is eight.

00:01:49.936 --> 00:01:54.010
So 1/8 times eight is one minus four.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.870
So that's going to be,
this is negative three.

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:59.520
And so we don't have a situation

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:04.040
where h at our higher
endpoint is actually larger.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.210
This is a negative average rate of change.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.010
So I'll rule this one out.

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.270
And actually just to
help us visualize this,

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:12.860
I did go to Desmos and
graph this function.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.490
And we can visually see that we have

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.300
a negative average rate of change

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.940
from x equals zero to x equals two.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.290
At x equals zero, this
is where our function is,

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:24.150
at x equals two, this is
where our function is,

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.740
and so you can see, at x equals two,

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.280
our function has a lower value.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.520
You could also think of
the average rate of change

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.630
as the slope of the line

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.460
that connects the two
endpoints on the function.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.500
And so you can see it
has a negative slope,

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.330
so we have a negative
average rate of change

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.060
between those two points.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.800
Now what about between these two?

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.740
So h of zero, we already
calculated as zero,

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.480
and what is h of eight?

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.060
Well, let's see that's 1/8

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.610
times eight to the third power.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:55.410
Well, if I do eight to third power,

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.160
but then divide by eight,
that's the same thing

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.380
as eight to the second power.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.130
So that's going to be 64

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.840
minus eight to the second power minus 64,

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.400
so that's equal to zero.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.280
So here we have a zero
average rate of change

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.880
'cause this numerator's going to be zero,

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:09.840
so we can rule that out.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.520
And you see it right over here.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.210
When x is equal to zero,
our function is there,

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.220
when x is equal to eight,
our function is there,

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:19.060
and you can see that the slope of the line

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:21.640
that connects those two points is zero.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.850
So you have zero average rate of change

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.690
between those two points.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.410
Now what about choice C?

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:30.150
So let's see, h of six

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.740
is going to be equal to

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:36.450
1/8 times six to the third power.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.890
So let's see, 36 times six is 180

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:43.203
plus 36, so that is going to be 216.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:48.740
216 minus 36,

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.480
216 is six times six times six,

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.130
and then if we divide that by eight,

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:56.880
that is going to be the same thing as,

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:01.830
this is 36, and then we have 6/8 of 36.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.850
So this is going to simplify

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:08.490
to 3/4 times 36 minus 36,

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.920
which is going to be
equal to negative nine.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.260
You could have done it with a calculator

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:13.640
or done some long division,

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.240
but hopefully what I just
did makes some sense.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:17.530
It's a little bit of arithmetic.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:22.020
And so, at h of six, we have
our function is negative nine,

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.410
and then h of eight, I'll draw a line here

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:25.890
so we don't make it too messy,

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:28.840
h of eight we already
know is equal to zero.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:31.410
So our function at this endpoint is higher

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:33.690
than the value of our
function at this endpoint.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.290
So we do have a positive
average rate of change.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.180
So I would pick that
choice right over there.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.820
And you could see it visually.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:43.000
h of six, when x is equal to six,

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.430
our value of our function
is negative nine.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.160
And when x is equal to eight,

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.920
our value of our function is zero.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:52.770
And so, the line that
connects those two points

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.810
definitely has a positive slope.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.060
So we have a positive
average rate of change

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.610
over that interval.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.300
Now, if we were just
doing this on our own,

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.720
we'd be done, but we could just

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.440
check this one right over here.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:08.060
If we compare h of zero,
we already know is zero,

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:11.670
and h of six, we already know
is equal to negative nine.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.830
So this is a negative
average rate of change

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.740
because at the higher
endpoint right over here,

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:18.860
we have a lower value of our function,

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:19.760
so we'd rule this out.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:20.660
And you see it right over here,

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:23.630
if you go from x equals
zero where the function is

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.970
to x equals six where the function is,

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.640
it looks something,

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.910
it looks something like that.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.810
Clearly that line has a negative slope.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.713
So we have a negative
average rate of change.

